    <description>

The Venera 3 Energetic Particles experiment was a Soviet suite of particle
detectors that monitored the flux of charged particles of medium energies in
interplanetary space during cruise and in the vicinity of Venus,
specifically measuring protons (&gt;30 MeV) from the sunward direction; and
protons (1-5 MeV) and electrons (0.05 MeV) perpendicular to the sunward
direction.

        </description>
